dEQP-GLES3 on ogles2 before all of ES 3.0 is in (docs/GLES3_PLAN.md stages B
and C): glu::resetState, after every case, checks glGetError after each part
of the state it resets, and an ES 3.0 setting the library does not take yet
(GL_PRIMITIVE_RESTART_FIXED_INDEX was the first) threw in the case's deinit,
which ends the run after one case. The error is logged and the run goes on;
the state of that part may stay as the case left it. Drop the patch once the
library takes all of ES 3.0's state (stage B item 13).

--- a/modules/gles3/tes3TestPackage.cpp
+++ b/modules/gles3/tes3TestPackage.cpp
@@ -79,7 +79,19 @@
     testCase->deinit();
 
     DE_ASSERT(m_testPackage.getContext());
-    glu::resetState(m_testPackage.getContext()->getRenderContext(), m_testPackage.getContext()->getContextInfo());
+    // ogles2: an ES 3.0 context before all of ES 3.0 is in (docs/GLES3_PLAN.md
+    // stages B and C) refuses some of the state resetState sets, and an error
+    // in a case's deinit ends the run. Logged, and the run goes on.
+    try
+    {
+        glu::resetState(m_testPackage.getContext()->getRenderContext(),
+                        m_testPackage.getContext()->getContextInfo());
+    }
+    catch (const tcu::TestError &e)
+    {
+        m_testPackage.getContext()->getTestContext().getLog()
+            << tcu::TestLog::Message << "ogles2: state reset incomplete: " << e.what() << tcu::TestLog::EndMessage;
+    }
 }
 
 tcu::TestNode::IterateResult TestCaseWrapper::iterate(tcu::TestCase *testCase)
